{{see also|North Carolina's 13th congressional district}}
The new 13th district includes all of [[Caswell County, North Carolina|Caswell]], [[Franklin County, North Carolina|Franklin]], [[Harnett County, North Carolina|Harnett]], [[Johnston County, North Carolina|Johnston]], [[Lee County, North Carolina|Lee]], and [[Person County, North Carolina|Person]] counties, as well as most of [[Granville County, North Carolina|Granville County]] and portions of [[Wake County, North Carolina|Wake County]]. The incumbent was Democrat [[Wiley Nickel]], who was first elected with 51.6% of the vote in 2022.<ref name="HPVT"/> On December 14, 2023, Nickel announced he would retire after one term in office.<ref>{{Cite news |last=McIntire |first=Mary Ellen |date=December 14, 2023 |title=Nickel won't run again for House, eyes 2026 Senate bid instead |url=https://rollcall.com/2023/12/14/nickel-wont-run-again-for-house-eyes-2026-senate-bid-instead/ |access-date=January 20, 2024 |work=[[Roll Call]]}}</ref>

