The new 14th district includes all of [[Burke County, North Carolina|Burke]], [[Cleveland County, North Carolina|Cleveland]], [[Gaston County, North Carolina|Gaston]], and [[Rutherford County, North Carolina|Rutherford]] counties, as well as portions of [[Mecklenburg County, North Carolina|Mecklenburg]] and [[Polk County, North Carolina|Polk]] counties. The incumbent was Democrat [[Jeff Jackson (politician)|Jeff Jackson]], who was first elected with 57.7% of the vote in 2022.<ref name="HPVT"/> On October 26, 2023, Jackson announced he would retire after one term, instead running for [[2024 North Carolina Attorney General election|Attorney General]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=McIntire |first=Mary Ellen |date=October 26, 2023 |title=GOP-drawn map spurs freshman Rep. Jeff Jackson to run for NC attorney general |url=https://rollcall.com/2023/10/26/gop-drawn-map-spurs-freshman-rep-jeff-jackson-to-run-for-nc-attorney-general/ |access-date=January 20, 2024 |work=[[Roll Call]]}}</ref>

